var __index = {"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"index.html","title":"Appian on Kubernetes Utilities","text":"<p>A set of Python CLI tools that accelerate deployment and management of Appian on Kubernetes (AoK) environments.</p>"},{"location":"index.html#whats-included","title":"What's Included","text":"Command Purpose <code>aok generate</code> Generates K8s manifests, SQL scripts, and a step-by-step DEPLOYMENT.md from a config-values YAML <code>aok visualize</code> Converts an Appian site CR into a K8s architecture diagram (PNG) <code>aok migration-convert</code> Parses Migration Tool draft YAML into Helm values for <code>appian-platform-cs</code>"},{"location":"index.html#quick-links","title":"Quick Links","text":"<ul> <li>Getting Started \u2014 prerequisites, installation, first run</li> <li>Usage \u2014 CLI examples for every subcommand</li> <li>Configuration \u2014 config-values YAML schema reference</li> </ul>"},{"location":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration Reference","text":"<p>This document describes the complete schema for the <code>config-values.yaml</code> file used by <code>aok generate</code>. The config-values file is the single input that drives all generated deployment artifacts.</p>"},{"location":"configuration.html#file-structure","title":"File Structure","text":"<p>The config-values file is a YAML document with three required top-level sections:</p> <pre><code>repository:\n  # Container registry settings\noperator:\n  # Appian Operator deployment settings\nsite:\n  # Appian site deployment settings\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"configuration.html#repository","title":"repository","text":"<p>Registry and authentication settings for pulling Appian container images and Helm charts.</p> Field Type Required Default Description <code>appian</code> string Yes \u2014 Container image registry path (e.g. <code>my-registry.com/appian/images</code>) <code>helm</code> string No \u2014 OCI Helm chart registry URL (e.g. <code>my-registry.com/appian/helm</code>) <code>authSecretName</code> string No \u2014 Name of an existing Kubernetes image pull secret <code>authUsername</code> string No \u2014 Registry authentication username (requires <code>authPassword</code>) <code>authPassword</code> string No \u2014 Registry authentication password (requires <code>authUsername</code>)"},{"location":"configuration.html#conditional-requirements","title":"Conditional Requirements","text":"<ul> <li>If <code>authUsername</code> is provided, <code>authPassword</code> must also be provided (and vice versa). These are used to generate a registry credential secret as part of the deployment guide.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"configuration.html#operator","title":"operator","text":"<p>Settings for deploying the Appian Operator.</p> Field Type Required Default Description <code>topology</code> string Yes \u2014 Operator deployment topology. Valid values: <code>cluster-wide</code>, <code>main-and-site</code> <code>webhookCertModel</code> string Yes \u2014 Webhook TLS certificate provisioning model. Valid values: <code>cert-manager</code>, <code>ca-bundle</code> <code>version</code> string Yes \u2014 Operator version tag (e.g. <code>v0.194.0</code>) <code>namespace</code> string No <code>appian-operator</code> Kubernetes namespace for the operator <code>caBundleBase64Value</code> string Conditional \u2014 Base64-encoded CA certificate bundle for webhook TLS"},{"location":"configuration.html#valid-values","title":"Valid Values","text":"<p>topology:</p> Value Description <code>cluster-wide</code> Single operator instance managing all namespaces <code>main-and-site</code> Separate main and site operators; avoids cross-namespace permissions <p>webhookCertModel:</p> Value Description <code>cert-manager</code> Automated TLS via cert-manager (must be pre-installed in the cluster) <code>ca-bundle</code> Manually provided CA bundle embedded in operator Helm values"},{"location":"configuration.html#conditional-requirements_1","title":"Conditional Requirements","text":"<ul> <li>When <code>webhookCertModel</code> is <code>ca-bundle</code>, the field <code>caBundleBase64Value</code> is required. This value is the base64-encoded CA certificate that the operator uses to validate webhook TLS connections.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"configuration.html#site","title":"site","text":"<p>Settings for the Appian site deployment.</p> Field Type Required Default Description <code>namespace</code> string Yes \u2014 Kubernetes namespace for the Appian site <code>name</code> string Yes \u2014 Appian site name (used in resource naming) <code>appianPlatformCsHelmChartVersion</code> string Yes \u2014 Version of the <code>appian-platform-cs</code> Helm chart <code>class</code> string Yes \u2014 Site sizing class. Valid values: <code>x-small</code>, <code>small</code>, <code>medium</code>, <code>large</code>, <code>x-large</code> <code>highAvailability</code> boolean No <code>false</code> Enable high-availability mode with multiple engine replicas <code>sharedStorage</code> boolean No <code>true</code> when HA Enable shared data PVC for the site <code>rwxStorageClassName</code> string Conditional \u2014 Kubernetes StorageClass name supporting ReadWriteMany access <code>smtpAuthPassword</code> string No \u2014 SMTP authentication password (written to <code>passwords.properties</code>) <code>dataSources</code> object No See below Database provisioning settings"},{"location":"configuration.html#valid-values_1","title":"Valid Values","text":"<p>class:</p> Value Description <code>x-small</code> Minimal resource allocation for development/testing <code>small</code> Low resource allocation for small workloads <code>medium</code> Moderate resource allocation for typical production <code>large</code> High resource allocation for demanding workloads <code>x-large</code> Maximum resource allocation for large-scale production"},{"location":"configuration.html#conditional-requirements_2","title":"Conditional Requirements","text":"<ul> <li>When <code>highAvailability</code> is <code>true</code> or <code>sharedStorage</code> is <code>true</code>, the field <code>rwxStorageClassName</code> is required. This must reference a StorageClass that supports <code>ReadWriteMany</code> access mode.</li> <li>When <code>highAvailability</code> is <code>true</code> and <code>sharedStorage</code> is not explicitly set, <code>sharedStorage</code> defaults to <code>true</code> (HA sites always require shared storage).</li> </ul>"},{"location":"configuration.html#sitedatasources","title":"site.dataSources","text":"<p>Database provisioning settings. These control the generated SQL script for creating database schemas and users.</p> Field Type Required Default Description <code>dbType</code> string No <code>mysql</code> Target database platform <code>primarySchemaName</code> string No <code>appian_primary</code> Primary database schema name <code>primaryUsername</code> string No <code>PRIMARY_DB_USERNAME</code> Primary database username <code>primaryPassword</code> string No <code>YOUR_PASSWORD_HERE</code> Primary database user password <code>businessUsername</code> string No \u2014 Business database username (triggers business DB provisioning) <code>businessPassword</code> string No <code>YOUR_PASSWORD_HERE</code> Business database user password <code>businessSchemaName</code> string No <code>appian</code> Business database schema name"},{"location":"configuration.html#valid-values_2","title":"Valid Values","text":"<p>dbType:</p> Value Description <code>mysql</code> MySQL 8.x <code>mariadb</code> MariaDB 10.x+ <code>oracle</code> Oracle Database <code>postgresql</code> PostgreSQL 12+ <code>sqlserver</code> Microsoft SQL Server <code>db2</code> IBM DB2"},{"location":"configuration.html#business-database-provisioning","title":"Business Database Provisioning","text":"<p>Business database statements are only included in the generated SQL script when <code>businessUsername</code> is provided. If <code>businessUsername</code> is set but <code>businessSchemaName</code> is omitted, the business schema defaults to <code>appian</code>.</p>"},{"location":"configuration.html#storage-sizing-by-class","title":"Storage Sizing by Class","text":"<p>The generator automatically determines PVC storage capacity based on the selected <code>site.class</code>. The following table shows the storage values used for each sizing class:</p> Class Shared Logs (non-HA) Shared Logs (HA) Shared Data (HA) Shared Data (non-HA) x-small 100Gi 200Gi 100Gi 50Gi small 100Gi 200Gi 100Gi 50Gi medium 150Gi 300Gi 200Gi 100Gi large 200Gi 400Gi 300Gi 150Gi x-large 200Gi 400Gi 300Gi 150Gi <p>Notes:</p> <ul> <li>The shared logs PVC (<code>appian-shared-logs</code>) is always generated. Its capacity is selected based on whether <code>highAvailability</code> is <code>true</code> (HA column) or <code>false</code> (non-HA column).</li> <li>The shared data PVC (<code>appian-shared-data</code>) is only generated when <code>sharedStorage</code> is <code>true</code>. Its capacity is selected based on the HA mode.</li> <li>Both PVCs use the <code>ReadWriteMany</code> access mode and reference the <code>rwxStorageClassName</code> value.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"configuration.html#conditional-requirements-summary","title":"Conditional Requirements Summary","text":"Condition Required Field <code>operator.webhookCertModel</code> is <code>ca-bundle</code> <code>operator.caBundleBase64Value</code> <code>site.highAvailability</code> is <code>true</code> <code>site.rwxStorageClassName</code> <code>site.sharedStorage</code> is <code>true</code> <code>site.rwxStorageClassName</code> <code>repository.authUsername</code> is provided <code>repository.authPassword</code> <code>repository.authPassword</code> is provided <code>repository.authUsername</code>"},{"location":"configuration.html#complete-example","title":"Complete Example","text":"<p>The following example shows all available fields:</p> <pre><code>repository:\n  appian: \"my-container-registry.com/appian/images\"\n  helm: \"my-container-registry.com/appian/helm\"\n  authSecretName: \"regcred\"\n  authUsername: \"AWS\"\n  authPassword: \"REGCRED_PWD_VAR_PLACEHOLDER\"\n\noperator:\n  topology: \"cluster-wide\"\n  webhookCertModel: \"ca-bundle\"\n  version: \"v0.194.0\"\n  namespace: \"appian-operator\"\n  caBundleBase64Value: \"LS0tLS1CRUdJTi...\"\n\nsite:\n  namespace: \"appian-site\"\n  name: \"company-proj-dev\"\n  appianPlatformCsHelmChartVersion: \"1.0.2\"\n  class: \"medium\"\n  highAvailability: true\n  sharedStorage: true\n  rwxStorageClassName: \"my.fileshare.sc\"\n  smtpAuthPassword: \"my_smtp_pwd\"\n  dataSources:\n    dbType: \"mysql\"\n    primarySchemaName: \"appian_primary\"\n    primaryUsername: \"appian_primary_user\"\n    primaryPassword: \"primary_password_here\"\n    businessUsername: \"appian_business_user\"\n    businessPassword: \"business_password_here\"\n    businessSchemaName: \"appian\"\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"getting-started.html","title":"Getting Started","text":""},{"location":"getting-started.html#prerequisites","title":"Prerequisites","text":"<ul> <li>Python 3.10 or later</li> <li>pip (included with Python)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#installation","title":"Installation","text":"<p>Your administrator will provide a zip file (e.g. <code>appian-kubernetes-utilities-3.0.1.zip</code>). Unzip it to find the wheel and offline docs:</p> <pre><code>unzip appian-kubernetes-utilities-x.y.z.zip\npip install appian_kubernetes_utilities-x.y.z-py3-none-any.whl\n</code></pre> <p>Replace <code>x.y.z</code> with the version you received (e.g. <code>3.0.1</code>).</p> <p>The <code>aok-utilities-docs/</code> folder contains the offline documentation \u2014 open <code>aok-utilities-docs/index.html</code> in your browser.</p> <p>For an isolated environment, you can also use pipx:</p> <pre><code>pipx install appian_kubernetes_utilities-x.y.z-py3-none-any.whl\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#verify-installation","title":"Verify Installation","text":"<p>Confirm the CLI is available:</p> <pre><code>aok --version\n</code></pre> <p>You should see output like:</p> <pre><code>aok 3.0.1\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#quick-start-aok-generate","title":"Quick Start \u2014 <code>aok generate</code>","text":"<p>Create a minimal <code>config-values.yaml</code>:</p> <pre><code>repository:\n  appian: my-registry.example.com/appian\n\noperator:\n  topology: cluster-wide\n  webhookCertModel: cert-manager\n  version: v0.194.0\n\nsite:\n  namespace: appian-site\n  name: my-site\n  appianPlatformCsHelmChartVersion: \"1.0.0\"\n  class: small\n  highAvailability: false\n  rwxStorageClassName: efs-sc\n</code></pre> <p>Run the generator:</p> <pre><code>aok generate -i config-values.yaml -o output/\n</code></pre> <p>This produces a <code>DEPLOYMENT.md</code> guide and Kubernetes manifests in the <code>output/</code> directory, ready for review and deployment.</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#non-python-prerequisites","title":"Non-Python Prerequisites","text":"<p>The following tools are not required by <code>aok</code> itself, but are referenced in the generated output:</p> Tool Referenced By Purpose Helm Generated <code>DEPLOYMENT.md</code> Helm commands for installing the Appian Operator and site charts kubectl Generated <code>DEPLOYMENT.md</code> Kubernetes commands for applying manifests and creating secrets Graphviz <code>aok visualize</code> subcommand Required at runtime by the <code>diagrams</code> library for PNG rendering <p>You only need these tools when you act on the generated instructions or use the visualizer \u2014 the generator itself runs without them.</p>"},{"location":"usage.html","title":"Usage","text":""},{"location":"usage.html#aok-generate","title":"<code>aok generate</code>","text":"<p>Generate AoK deployment manifests and a step-by-step deployment guide from a config-values YAML file.</p> <pre><code>aok generate -i &lt;config-values.yaml&gt; -o &lt;output-dir&gt; [--clean] [--debug]\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"usage.html#options","title":"Options","text":"Option Short Required Description <code>--input</code> <code>-i</code> Yes Path to the config-values YAML file <code>--output</code> <code>-o</code> Yes Path to the output directory (created if it does not exist) <code>--clean</code> <code>-c</code> No Remove all existing files in the output directory before generating <code>--debug</code> <code>-d</code> No Enable verbose diagnostic output (sets log level to DEBUG)"},{"location":"usage.html#minimal-config-values-example","title":"Minimal Config-Values Example","text":"<p>The smallest valid input for a non-HA, cluster-wide deployment using cert-manager:</p> <pre><code>repository:\n  appian: my-registry.example.com/appian\n\noperator:\n  topology: cluster-wide\n  webhookCertModel: cert-manager\n  version: v0.194.0\n\nsite:\n  namespace: appian-site\n  name: my-site\n  appianPlatformCsHelmChartVersion: \"1.0.0\"\n  class: small\n  highAvailability: false\n  rwxStorageClassName: efs-sc\n</code></pre> <p>Run:</p> <pre><code>aok generate -i config-values.yaml -o my-output/\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"usage.html#full-config-values-example","title":"Full Config-Values Example","text":"<p>A complete input covering all optional fields \u2014 HA mode, CA bundle webhook model, registry credentials, database configuration, and SMTP:</p> <pre><code>repository:\n  appian: \"my-container-registry.com/appian/images\"\n  helm: \"my-container-registry.com/appian/helm\"\n  authSecretName: \"regcred\"\n  authUsername: \"AWS\"\n  authPassword: \"REGCRED_PWD_VAR_PLACEHOLDER\"\n\noperator:\n  topology: \"cluster-wide\"\n  webhookCertModel: \"ca-bundle\"\n  caBundleBase64Value: \"LS0tLS1CRUdJTi...\"\n  version: \"v0.194.0\"\n  namespace: \"custom-operator-ns\"\n\nsite:\n  namespace: \"appian-site\"\n  name: \"company-proj-prod\"\n  appianPlatformCsHelmChartVersion: \"1.0.2\"\n  highAvailability: true\n  class: \"medium\"\n  rwxStorageClassName: \"my.fileshare.sc\"\n  sharedStorage: true\n  smtpAuthPassword: \"my_smtp_pwd\"\n  dataSources:\n    dbType: \"postgresql\"\n    primarySchemaName: \"appian_primary\"\n    primaryUsername: \"appian_primary_user\"\n    primaryPassword: \"primary_password_here\"\n    businessUsername: \"appian_business_user\"\n    businessPassword: \"business_password_here\"\n    businessSchemaName: \"appian_business\"\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"usage.html#output-directory-structure","title":"Output Directory Structure","text":"<p>After running the generator, the output directory contains:</p> <pre><code>my-output/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 DEPLOYMENT.md                          # Step-by-step deployment guide\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 manifests/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 operator-values.yaml              # Operator Helm values\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 site-operator-values.yaml         # (main-and-site topology only)\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 cert-manager-selfsigned-cluster-issuer.yaml   # (cert-manager only)\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 cert-manager-appian-op-webhooks-cert-secret.yaml  # (cert-manager only)\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 appian-shared-logs-pvc.yaml       # Shared logs PVC\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 appian-shared-data-pvc.yaml       # (shared storage only)\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 appian-dbs-&lt;dbType&gt;.sql           # Database provisioning script\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 passwords.properties              # SMTP credentials\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 appian-platform-cs-values.yaml    # Draft Helm values for site chart\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 dependencies/                          # Reserved for future use\n</code></pre> <p>Files are generated conditionally based on your configuration:</p> <ul> <li><code>site-operator-values.yaml</code> \u2014 only when <code>operator.topology</code> is <code>main-and-site</code></li> <li><code>cert-manager-*.yaml</code> \u2014 only when <code>operator.webhookCertModel</code> is <code>cert-manager</code></li> <li><code>appian-shared-data-pvc.yaml</code> \u2014 only when <code>site.sharedStorage</code> is <code>true</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"usage.html#using-clean","title":"Using <code>--clean</code>","text":"<p>The <code>--clean</code> flag removes all existing files in the output directory before generating new ones. This is useful when you change your configuration and want to ensure no stale files remain from a previous run.</p> <p>Without <code>--clean</code>, existing files that match generated filenames are overwritten, but other files are left untouched.</p> <pre><code># First run \u2014 generates output\naok generate -i config-values.yaml -o output/\n\n# Configuration changed (e.g. switched from cert-manager to ca-bundle)\n# Use --clean to remove stale cert-manager manifests\naok generate -i config-values.yaml -o output/ --clean\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"usage.html#using-debug","title":"Using <code>--debug</code>","text":"<p>The <code>--debug</code> flag enables verbose logging to stderr, showing each step of the generation pipeline. Useful for troubleshooting template rendering or validation issues.</p> <pre><code>aok generate -i config-values.yaml -o output/ --debug\n</code></pre> <p>Example debug output:</p> <pre><code>DEBUG    aok_utilities.generator.core: Loading config from config-values.yaml\nDEBUG    aok_utilities.generator.config: Validating schema...\nDEBUG    aok_utilities.generator.config: Resolving defaults: dbType=mysql, namespace=appian-operator\nDEBUG    aok_utilities.generator.storage: Loading storage values for class=small\nDEBUG    aok_utilities.generator.template_selector: Selected 7 templates for rendering\nDEBUG    aok_utilities.generator.renderer: Rendering operator-values.yaml.j2 \u2192 manifests/operator-values.yaml\nDEBUG    aok_utilities.generator.renderer: Rendering DEPLOYMENT.md.j2 \u2192 DEPLOYMENT.md\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"usage.html#error-output-examples","title":"Error Output Examples","text":""},{"location":"usage.html#missing-required-fields","title":"Missing required fields","text":"<pre><code>$ aok generate -i incomplete.yaml -o output/\n</code></pre> <pre><code>ERROR    Configuration validation failed:\nERROR      \u2022 operator.topology: required field is missing\nERROR      \u2022 site.namespace: required field is missing\nERROR      \u2022 site.class: required field is missing\n</code></pre> <p>Exit code: <code>1</code></p>"},{"location":"usage.html#invalid-enumeration-value","title":"Invalid enumeration value","text":"<pre><code>$ aok generate -i bad-topology.yaml -o output/\n</code></pre> <pre><code>ERROR    Configuration validation failed:\nERROR      \u2022 operator.topology: invalid value 'single-node'; valid options are: cluster-wide, main-and-site\n</code></pre> <p>Exit code: <code>1</code></p>"},{"location":"usage.html#invalid-yaml-syntax","title":"Invalid YAML syntax","text":"<pre><code>$ aok generate -i malformed.yaml -o output/\n</code></pre> <pre><code>ERROR    Cannot read config file: malformed.yaml: YAML syntax error at line 12: mapping values are not allowed here\n</code></pre> <p>Exit code: <code>1</code></p>"},{"location":"usage.html#file-not-found","title":"File not found","text":"<pre><code>$ aok generate -i nonexistent.yaml -o output/\n</code></pre> <pre><code>ERROR    Cannot read config file: nonexistent.yaml: file not found\n</code></pre> <p>Exit code: <code>1</code></p>"},{"location":"usage.html#conditional-validation-failure","title":"Conditional validation failure","text":"<pre><code>$ aok generate -i missing-ca-bundle.yaml -o output/\n</code></pre> <p>Where <code>missing-ca-bundle.yaml</code> has <code>operator.webhookCertModel: ca-bundle</code> but no <code>caBundleBase64Value</code>:</p> <pre><code>ERROR    Configuration validation failed:\nERROR      \u2022 operator.caBundleBase64Value: required because operator.webhookCertModel is 'ca-bundle'\n</code></pre> <p>Exit code: <code>1</code></p>"},{"location":"usage.html#aok-visualize","title":"<code>aok visualize</code>","text":"<p>Read an Appian site YAML (the Kubernetes Custom Resource for an Appian site) and generate a PNG architecture diagram showing pods, PVCs, services, ingress, databases, and SMTP connectivity. A text-based resource summary table is also printed to stdout.</p> <pre><code>aok visualize -i &lt;site.yaml&gt; [-o &lt;output-path&gt;] [--debug]\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"usage.html#prerequisites","title":"Prerequisites","text":"<p>The <code>diagrams</code> Python library renders diagrams via Graphviz. You must install Graphviz before running <code>aok visualize</code>:</p> Platform Command macOS <code>brew install graphviz</code> Windows <code>choco install graphviz</code> or <code>winget install graphviz</code> Debian/Ubuntu <code>sudo apt install graphviz</code> <p>If Graphviz is not installed, the command exits with a clear error message and installation instructions.</p>"},{"location":"usage.html#options_1","title":"Options","text":"Option Short Required Description <code>--input</code> <code>-i</code> Yes Path to the Appian site YAML file (Custom Resource) <code>--output</code> <code>-o</code> No Output path for the generated PNG (default: <code>./appian_site_visualisation</code>) <code>--debug</code> <code>-d</code> No Enable verbose diagnostic output (sets log level to DEBUG) <p>Note: The <code>diagrams</code> library automatically appends <code>.png</code> to the output path. If you specify <code>--output my-diagram</code>, the generated file will be <code>my-diagram.png</code>.</p>"},{"location":"usage.html#example-commands","title":"Example Commands","text":"<pre><code># Basic usage \u2014 generates ./appian_site_visualisation.png\naok visualize -i my-site.yaml\n\n# Custom output path \u2014 generates ./docs/architecture.png\naok visualize -i my-site.yaml -o ./docs/architecture\n\n# With debug logging\naok visualize -i my-site.yaml -o ./docs/architecture --debug\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"usage.html#generating-input-from-helm-values","title":"Generating Input from Helm Values","text":"<p>If you deploy your Appian site using the <code>appian-platform-cs</code> Helm chart, you can generate the input YAML with <code>helm template</code>:</p> <pre><code>helm template my-site appian-platform-cs/ -f my-values.yaml &gt; rendered-site.yaml\naok visualize -i rendered-site.yaml -o my-site-diagram\n</code></pre> <p>This renders the Custom Resource manifest from your Helm values without applying it to a cluster.</p>"},{"location":"usage.html#output","title":"Output","text":"<p>The command produces two outputs:</p> <ol> <li>PNG diagram \u2014 An architecture diagram saved to the output path (with <code>.png</code> extension). The diagram shows:</li> <li>All AoK component pods (zookeeper, kafka, searchServer, dataServer, serviceManager, webapp, httpd) with per-pod resource allocations</li> <li>PVC nodes for each component's storage</li> <li>Shared storage (health check logs, HA data)</li> <li>Service Manager engine breakdown per replica with per-engine resources</li> <li>K8s Service and ingress configuration (with platform-specific icons for ALB, Azure App Gateway, Nginx)</li> <li>Database nodes with type-specific icons connected via JDBC</li> <li>SMTP server connectivity</li> <li> <p>A Users node showing site URLs</p> </li> <li> <p>Resource summary table (printed to stdout) \u2014 A tabular breakdown of CPU, memory, and storage allocations per component plus site-wide totals.</p> </li> </ol>"},{"location":"usage.html#error-output-examples_1","title":"Error Output Examples","text":""},{"location":"usage.html#graphviz-not-installed","title":"Graphviz not installed","text":"<pre><code>$ aok visualize -i my-site.yaml\n</code></pre> <pre><code>ERROR    Graphviz is required for diagram generation.\n         Install Graphviz to generate diagrams:\n           macOS:         brew install graphviz\n           Windows:       choco install graphviz  (or)  winget install graphviz\n           Debian/Ubuntu: sudo apt install graphviz\n</code></pre> <p>Exit code: <code>1</code></p>"},{"location":"usage.html#input-file-not-found","title":"Input file not found","text":"<pre><code>$ aok visualize -i nonexistent.yaml\n</code></pre> <pre><code>ERROR    Cannot read config file: nonexistent.yaml: file not found\n</code></pre> <p>Exit code: <code>1</code></p>"},{"location":"usage.html#invalid-yaml-syntax_1","title":"Invalid YAML syntax","text":"<pre><code>$ aok visualize -i malformed.yaml\n</code></pre> <pre><code>ERROR    Cannot read config file: malformed.yaml: YAML syntax error\n</code></pre> <p>Exit code: <code>1</code></p>"},{"location":"usage.html#output-directory-does-not-exist","title":"Output directory does not exist","text":"<pre><code>$ aok visualize -i my-site.yaml -o /nonexistent/path/diagram\n</code></pre> <pre><code>ERROR    Output directory not found: /nonexistent/path\n</code></pre> <p>Exit code: <code>1</code></p>"},{"location":"usage.html#aok-migration-convert","title":"<code>aok migration-convert</code>","text":"<p>Convert a Migration Tool draft site YAML into a Helm values file for the <code>appian-platform-cs</code> chart. The converter parses the input, validates it for non-standard or deprecated configurations, and emits a clean values file with inline comments and action annotations.</p> <pre><code>aok migration-convert -i &lt;draft-site.yaml&gt; [-o &lt;output-values.yaml&gt;] [--debug]\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"usage.html#options_2","title":"Options","text":"Option Short Required Description <code>--input</code> <code>-i</code> Yes Path to the Migration Tool draft site YAML file <code>--output</code> <code>-o</code> No Output Helm values file path (default: <code>appian-platform-cs-values.yaml</code>) <code>--debug</code> No Enable verbose diagnostic output (sets log level to DEBUG)"},{"location":"usage.html#what-it-does","title":"What It Does","text":"<ol> <li>Parses the Migration Tool draft site YAML (apiVersion <code>crd.k8s.appian.com/v1beta1</code>, kind <code>Appian</code>)</li> <li>Extracts site URL, version, HA mode, component replicas, engine overrides, data sources, and custom properties</li> <li>Partitions custom properties into enforced properties (mapped to dedicated Helm keys), SMTP configuration, and additional custom properties</li> <li>Validates the configuration, emitting warnings for non-standard replica counts, deprecated properties, unsupported JDBC drivers, etc.</li> <li>Emits a complete Helm values YAML with inline comments indicating what the user needs to update, what must not be changed, and what was detected as non-standard</li> </ol>"},{"location":"usage.html#example","title":"Example","text":"<pre><code>aok migration-convert -i migration-draft-site.yaml -o my-site-values.yaml\n</code></pre> <p>Output on success:</p> <pre><code>  \u2022 conf.search-server.user.appian.password is now managed by the Operator from v0.181.0 and has been removed from the output.\n  \u2022 Data source factories must be changed to org.apache.tomcat.jdbc.pool.DataSourceFactory with passwords provided via passwordSecretKeyRef.\nWrote my-site-values.yaml (2 warnings)\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"usage.html#output-file-structure","title":"Output File Structure","text":"<p>The generated values file includes these sections in order:</p> Section Description Header comment Generator version, chart reference Warnings block Bullet-pointed validation warnings (if any) <code>siteName</code> Empty placeholder \u2014 user must provide <code>version</code> Extracted from input \u2014 DO NOT CHANGE <code>url</code> Site URL from input <code>staticUrl</code> / <code>dynamicUrl</code> If present in input <code>class</code> Empty placeholder \u2014 user selects sizing class <code>highAvailability</code> Derived from zookeeper replicas \u2014 DO NOT CHANGE <code>cascadeVersionToComponentTags</code> Always <code>true</code> \u2014 DO NOT CHANGE <code>passwordsPropertiesSecretName</code> Only if SMTP auth is enabled <code>metricsAuthToken</code> If present in custom properties <code>smtp</code> SMTP configuration (if SMTP properties were present) <code>additionalCustomProperties</code> All non-enforced, non-SMTP, non-removed properties <code>license</code> Default license secret/configmap names <code>storage</code> Storage class and PVC placeholders <code>images</code> Image repository placeholders Component overrides Only for components with non-default values <code>ingressTemplate</code> Ingress configuration placeholder"},{"location":"usage.html#validation-warnings","title":"Validation Warnings","text":"<p>The converter checks for and warns about:</p> <ul> <li>Analytics shard count exceeding 3</li> <li><code>MAX_EXEC_ENGINE_LOAD_METRIC</code> exceeding 2145</li> <li>Deprecated/removed properties (search-server password, RTS circuit breaker)</li> <li>Component replica counts deviating from HA/non-HA defaults</li> <li>Non-standard webapp, serviceManager, or engine override replica counts</li> <li>Non-suite <code>applicationContext</code></li> <li>JDBC drivers not shipped with the platform (mysql, mysql:aws, db2)</li> <li>Data source factory requiring migration to Tomcat pool</li> </ul>"},{"location":"usage.html#error-handling","title":"Error Handling","text":"Scenario Behaviour Input file not found Prints error to stderr, exits with code 1 Input file not readable Prints error to stderr, exits with code 1 Invalid YAML syntax Prints error to stderr, exits with code 1 Malformed version string Prints error to stderr, exits with code 1 Output path not writable Prints error to stderr, exits with code 1"},{"location":"usage.html#using-debug_1","title":"Using <code>--debug</code>","text":"<pre><code>aok migration-convert -i draft-site.yaml --debug\n</code></pre> <p>Enables DEBUG-level logging showing each step of the parse \u2192 validate \u2192 emit pipeline.</p>"}]}